# beta-review: secrets and host artifacts must never enter an image. The
# release workflow builds from a clean CI checkout, but `install.sh` and
# local compose builds use the operator's working tree — which holds the
# TLS private key (certbot), `lfctl backup` dumps, and possibly the
# release signing key. `/app` is readable by every in-container process,
# including the plugin worker.
infra/keys
infra/certbot
backups
# security-review INFRA-002: configs rendered by install.sh /
# render-configs.sh carry the TURN shared secret (and the operator's
# domain); install.sh renders them into the working tree right before
# `up -d --build`, and the plugin worker runs this same image. The image
# only needs infra/update (manifests + release public key).
infra/turn/turnserver.conf
infra/livekit/livekit.yaml
infra/nginx/conf.d/*.conf
.install-staging*
**/*.log
**/*.dump
**/*.pem
!infra/update/release-public.pem
**/*.key
# Build artifacts / caches that only bloat the context (src-tauri/target
# alone is several GB of Rust output).
apps/desktop/src-tauri/target
.pnpm-store
.test
.rc*.log
coverage
**/coverage
